    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n55540" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κατά-φρακτος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>covered, shut up</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐν δεσμῷ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>Ant.</u>
					958
				</span></i>
			 (lyr., in old 
				Att.
			 form <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κατάφαρκτος</span></b> ); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πλοῖα κ.</span>
			<i>decked</i> vessels, <i><span class="en">
				Th.
				1.10
			</span></i> codd., cf. <i><span class="en">
				Plb.
				1.20.13
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔν τε ταῖς ἀφράκτοις καὶ ταῖς κ.
					ναυσί</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>IG</u>
					12(1).41
				</span></i>
			 (Rhodes, <span class="entity">i B.C.</span>); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡ κ.
				ἵππος</span> cavalry <i>clad in full armour, mailed</i>,
				<i><span class="en">
				Plb.
				30.25.9
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Arr.
				<u>Tact.</u>
				4.1
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				19.4
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἱππεῖς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					<u>Crass.</u>
					21
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰκ</span>. <i>coat of mail,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				PMagd.
				13.6
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(iii B.C.)</span>: metaph., <i>encased</i> in ignorance of
			the future, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ψυχαί</span> Ion Trag.<i><span class="en">
				6
			</span></i>.</div>
